        -:    3:// Models the UE lifecycle a gNB-CU-CP performs: attach (create -> setup), signaling
        -:    4:// activity, bearer setup (add_drb), handover (begin_reconfigure -> complete/abort),
        -:    5:// and release (detach). The generator is a pure, deterministic function of
        -:    6:// (active_ues, seed): it keeps a lightweight per-slot expected-state model so every
        -:    7:// emitted op is valid by construction, and it advances that model optimistically so
        -:    8:// the *sequence of op kinds* is identical in C++ and Rust for the same parameters.
        -:    9:// That makes the per-kind op counts a cross-language parity signal.
        -:   10://
        -:   11:// PRNG draw order (MUST match the Rust generator exactly):
        -:   12://   1 draw  -> slot = next() % active_ues
        -:   13://   + if the slot is Connected or Reconfiguring: 1 more draw for the action roll.
        -:   14:// Empty/Idle slots consume no action draw (their transition is forced).
